          Andrea Giovannetti
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Prometeo's Charm spell fizzled and Prometeo wound up with his 
face covered with psycho-kinetic goo.
  Cantia was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Cantia.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Prometeo boldly marched his 
forces into Marzuq (#303).
  Girard's Oratory spell backfired and Girard wound up with his face covered 
with psycho-kinetic slime.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  Prometeo was 
tutored in Necromancy by Girard.  Prometeo practiced his Necromancy and his 
skill in Necromancy went up.
  During fall, Prometeo marched his forces into Shasta (#304).  Looking to 
the southeast, one espies a poor Mountain area, which is known as Moongard 
(#405).  It is populated by Orcs and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules 
there.  Their Orcish warriors traditionally array themselves in the style of 
Axemen and Heavy Cavalry.

  An army coming from the empire of Prometeo entered Shasta, hoping to 
subjugate that province ruled by the provincial Eagle chieftain and made up 
of extensive Mountains.  Prometeo was in command of the invading armies.  
The defenders were commanded by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  The armies 
were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Shasta (0304):

