  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with his warriors was Prometeo.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the provincial Eagle chieftain.
  Prometeo approached the gullible local commander under a flag of truce and 
glibly told him that the war was over, and under the treaty's terms, a large 
bridge was to be left unguarded, thus capturing this crucial bridge.  Also, 
his clever tactical planning assured his side a clear superiority.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 231st Legion were arrayed against the 
Veteran 30th Eagles.  The 262nd Heavy Cavalry flanked the undermanned enemy 
lines and attacked with full force.  The 30th Eagles swooped down on the 
231st Legion and attacked without mercy.  On this field, the 30th Eagles 
charged forward energetically, but failed to consider the unusually hot 
weather.  Their charge had little effect, except to tire them considerably.
  But would defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The 231st 
Legion bravely charged their enemy, but became strung out and were thrown 
back by a well-timed, effective countercharge.  Still, the 231st Legion 
fought the 30th Eagles and gradually shoved them back.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Prometeo as they broke 
through at a critical moment.
  Though Prometeo's host were triumphant, the provincial Eagle chieftain 
regrouped its men and decided to contest Shasta.  Prometeo's experience 
raised his prowess in Tactics.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Prometeo could not recruit 
Eagles in Shasta because Prometeo does not own that province, and 
mercenaries weren't available.  So, Prometeo discovered nothing valuable in 
his sagely researches.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  
Prometeo treated with his ally Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo 
treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Ashley (#74) has arrived in Mare Imbrium from Balmwood, attracted by the 
great (or infamous?  ?)   reputation of its king.

  Cantia was raided by the Werewolf, who came from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 42 gold in revenue.  11 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 46th Dragons trained well and improved in quality.  26 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left with 43 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Mortimer, Squire to Tarsus
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into spring.  Tarsus enlisted the 46th Dragons in 
Alderwood to serve Tarsus.
  During early summer, Tarsus flew over to Mare Imbrium.
  Tarsus's forces conquered Mare Imbrium without any major battles.  Mare 
Imbrium was found to have an income of 1 gold.
  With the advent of the late summer season Tarsus rode his flying armies 
over to Darkwood.  Southwest of here is Maicuru (#1804), a Jungle province 
owned by Giovanna d'Arco, where Humans dwell.  Their Human fighters array 
themselves in the style of Legion.  To the west there is a Forest province 
known as Marigold (#1803), a poor land of Humans where Giovanna d'Arco 
reigns.  Their Human warriors prefer to fight as Legion.
  Tarsus's naval forces took possession of Darkwood practically uncontested. 
Darkwood was found to have an income of 1 gold.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  Tarsus rode his flying armies 
into Waterford.
  Waterford was conquered and occupied by Tarsus's fleet.  Waterford was 
discovered to have an income of 1 gold.
  During early winter, Tarsus failed in his ineffectual attempt to cast a 
Bless spell.
  While carousing with fellow travellers in a tavern, Tarsus heard of a 
feature in Abu Matariq (#106): a Catacombs occupied by the Hydra, who guards 
the Longbow of Accuracy.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Tarsus


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I was tutored in the art of Sageness by Indra.  I practiced my 
Sageness and improved noticeably.  I invented nothing in my sagely 
researches.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I rode into Abu Matariq.  
Viewing the southeastern horizon, a man can see a rich Mountain province 
known as Kiska (#207).  It is said that Bradipo I reigns there.  It is known 
to be populated by Eagles.  If need be, they can call on a host of Eagles to 
defend their province.  Southwest of here lies the province of Jadegate 
(#107), ruled by Agesilao.  It is said to be a Mountain province occupied by 
Humans.  Their Human warriors array themselves in the style of Bowmen.  To 
the west lies a Desert area called Apurimac (#1806), populated by Dwarves.  
It is ruled by Agesilao.  Their Dwarven fighters array themselves in the 
style of Axemen and Camel Corps.  I was told by some sheepherders of a 
perilous feature in Abu Matariq previously unknown to us, an Ancient 
Megaliths (#68) where dwells the Renegade Necromancer.  What treasure may 
lie there is unknown.  Frightened peasants speak of the Renegade Necromancer 
in fear, describing him as an outlaw Necromancer who builds his fortunes on 
his dark power over life and death.  While adventuring, I saw no marauding 
monster.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer arrived.  I moved into Kiska.  
Looking to the east, one espies a poor Plain area, which is known as Kaluga 
(#307).  It is populated by Elves and Circe rules there.  Their Elven 
fighters traditionally array themselves as Bowmen.  Southeast of here is 
Khalturin (#208), a rich Plain province owned by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where Humans dwell.  Their Human fighters 
traditionally array themselves in the style of Legion and Light Cavalry.  To 
the southwest there is a Forest province known as Katmai (#108), a land of 
Elves where Agesilao rules.  Their Elven fighters traditionally array 
themselves in the style of Bowmen.  While adventuring, I encountered no 
monsters.
  During fall, I practiced my White Magic diligently for many weeks, but 
could make no headway.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I journeyed to Abu Matariq.  I 
saw no wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into spring, and Ishtar prepared to carry out his 
imperial assignments.  He tried hard to improve his Druidism, but he 
practiced in vain.
  During early summer, Ishtar was tutored in Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar 
studied and practiced his Sageness and his skill in Sageness went up.  He 
discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Ishtar was tutored in the art 
of Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar practiced diligently for months and his skill 
in Sageness increased.  He discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Ishtar was 
instructed in Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar practiced enthusiastically and 
improved his ability in Sageness.  He invented nothing worthy of note in his 
sagely experiments.
  In early winter, Ishtar was tutored in Sageness by Indra.  Ishtar 
rehearsed and practiced his Sageness and improved substantially.  He 
discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I cast a Plague spell.  Shasta was hit by a plague.  The Plague 
affected no armies in Shasta.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Girard's Oratory spell 
backfired and I wound up with my face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I worked on my 
Necromancy but was thwarted in my efforts.
  I heard a rumor telling of a perilous feature in Alderwood (#101), an 
Ancient Megaliths where dwells the Giant Amoeba.  The Ancient Megaliths is 
reputed to contain the Psychic Flail.
  During fall, I moved into Shasta.
  With the advent of the early winter season I wandered freely in Shasta, 
uncovering its mysteries, and raising our exploration level in Shasta to 30%.
I encountered no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Girard


